        <mxCell id="c27" value="&lt;i&gt;Both merges are left outer merges, so no invoice is dropped. The row count after loading is the test: compare it with the 20,914 invoices. Merging on a key that repeats in the second table gives the invoice one row for each match, here one for each shipment of its order, and every total on the invoice then counts twice or more. Amber cells: the invoice number repeated by the merge.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="417" width="860" height="52" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
